{"text":"DEQueue:\n\n[ _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _ ]\n  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7\nhead=0, tail=0\n\n\nhead = (head - 1) & mask;   // (0-1)&7 = 7\nes[head] = e;                // es[7] = A\n[ _, _, _, _, _, _, _, A ]\n  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7\nhead=7, tail=0\n\n\n\nhead = (head - 1) & mask;   // (7-1)&7 = 6\nes[head] = e;                // es[6] = B\n[ _, _, _, _, _, _, B, A ]\n  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7\nhead=6, tail=0\n\nes[tail] = e;                // es[0] = C\ntail = (tail + 1) & mask;   // (0+1)&7 = 1\n[ C, _, _, _, _, _, B, A ]\n  0  1  2  3  4  5  6  7\nhead=6, tail=1\n_____________________________________\n\n2.3 Rekursion über Daten\n\n\n\n\n","canvas":"data:image/png;base64,"}